OL,3,GNEWSA'Cracker of a comedian' - Frank
OL,4,ACarson commemorated on his centenary
OL,5,
OL,6,FWith his non-stop gags and catchphrases
OL,7,Flike "it's a cracker!", Frank Carson
OL,8,Frose to fame in the 1960s after winning
OL,9,Ftalent show Opportunity Knocks three
OL,10,Ftimes.
OL,12,FThe Belfast-born comedian became a
OL,13,Fhousehold name with the TV show The
OL,14,FComedians in the 1970s, alongside the
OL,15,Flikes of Charlie Williams, Bernard
OL,16,FManning and Jim Bowen.
OL,18,FOn Friday, he will be honoured at the
OL,19,Fformer St Patrick's National School,
OL,20,Fbeside St Patrick's Church on Donegall
OL,21,FStreet in Belfast, on what would have
OL,22,Fbeen his 100th birthday.
OL,23,APub: 06-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
